develops filtration technologies, including filtration media, filter element formation, filtration systems integration; and service-related solutions, such as remote digital diagnostic and prognostic platforms, and analytics. Atmus Filtration Technologies Inc. was founded in 1958 and is headquartered in Nashville, Tennessee.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Stephanie Juanita Disher | CEO, President & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $392K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $33K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Atmus Filtration Technologies I is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $4.1B market cap on $1.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 37% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 28-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 28%.","The business throws off $149M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.98\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 9.0\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.9%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.1\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (80% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.2},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 22% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 9% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Atmus Filtration (ATMU) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/atmus-filtration-atmu-q3-2026-191428000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793993243.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.361,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["